From 9ab6279c45bd3b823725b27a0f11d3bd730d5bfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jatniel <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:56:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Apply the touch layout's size, opacity and hidden controls,
 and the notch

Each control is drawn and hit at the size and opacity the player set: Layout
gives every control its own art pixel (the screen's, times the global scale,
times its own) and the Pen draws the control with it and with its alpha, so
plates, icons, the joystick and the key caps follow. A control grows from its
corner towards the screen, never past half the screen's height and never under
its default size.

Jump, Shift, Chat and the key caps can be hidden: they are not drawn and take
no touch. The D-pad, Pause and Back can't, whatever a file says, because
without them a player can't move or leave a menu.

On iOS the game now reads the window's safe area insets (winit's
WindowExtIOS::safe_area_insets) whenever it lays the controls out, so they
keep clear of the notch, the rounded corners and the home indicator, and it
follows the device as it turns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
